# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/

# Environment variables
.env

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Data
# ANCHORED with a leading slash — deliberately. Unanchored `data/` matches at
# ANY depth, so it silently swallowed every subtool's data directory too.
# world-showcase already had to work around it with a `!public/data/` negation
# (see world-showcase/.gitignore), and it would have hidden
# tools/fleet-devtools/' data/{jobs,artifacts}/.gitkeep. Note a nested
# negation only rescues a path if
# it un-excludes the DIRECTORY — git never descends into an excluded directory,
# so `!data/jobs/.gitkeep` alone would not have worked.
# This still ignores the fleet's own ./data (which holds real secrets — see the
# backup note below). Keep the slash.
/data/

# Timestamped backups of data/ and config — these can contain real secrets
# (e.g. data.backup-*/llm-settings.json holds plaintext provider API keys).
# Never let `git add -A` stage them.
data.backup-*/
config.yml.bak-*
*.bak-*

# Claude
# CLAUDE.md is deliberately tracked (private repo, 2026-08-07): it is the
# project brief agents and humans read first, and keeping it untracked meant
# corrections lived on one clone and never reached the deploy host. Verified
# free of credential values before tracking — it names env vars, never sets
# them. .claude/ stays ignored (per-machine session state).
.claude/
diagnostics/

# Generated town schematics (per-town runtime artifacts)
schematics/town_*/

# Python bytecode from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/buildops/

# Generated masterplan PDF exports. 409 MB across five files as of 2026-08-07,
# and git never sheds a large blob without a history rewrite — every future
# clone would pay for them forever. They are regenerable from the masterplan
# sources in docs/masterplans/. If these ever need versioning, use Git LFS
# rather than removing this rule.
docs/_pdfs/
